        "Nigerian schools, whether running WAEC/NECO, Cambridge or IB, typically follow a three-term year from September to July, with roughly a month's break between the first and second terms around Christmas and a shorter break around Easter. WASSCE and NECO sit in the second half of the academic year, generally April through June, with results released over the following months; Cambridge's main series runs May/June with a smaller October/November sitting some schools use for resits or accelerated candidates; JAMB's UTME is typically held early in the year, ahead of the WASSCE results that later combine with it. A tutoring plan built around these dates, rather than a generic school-year calendar, avoids wasted revision time.",
